---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import fontAwesomeLicense from '../../../LICENSES/LicenseRef-FontAwesome-Free.txt?raw';
import octiconsLicense from '../../../LICENSES/LicenseRef-Octicons-MIT.txt?raw';
import logos from '../assets/logos/catalog.json';
---
<Base title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Read-only package monitoring for <a href="https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/openRuyi">openRuyi</a>, a rolling Linux distribution for RISC-V.</p>

    <h2>Reading the table</h2>
    <dl class="api-list">
      <dt>Version</dt>
      <dd>The RPM-expanded SPEC version, followed by a green arrow when a newer upstream release is tracked. Comparison uses VERSION, not Epoch or Release.</dd>
      <dt>Build confirmation</dt>
      <dd>Red means the current source has not succeeded on every active target. A check mark belongs to its OBS target, not a release guarantee. A previous successful version appears below a result only when it cannot be inferred from the current version.</dd>
      <dt>Untracked</dt>
      <dd>No upstream version track configured. Other monitors do not affect version coverage.</dd>
      <dt>CheckFailed</dt>
      <dd>At least one collection check failed, including partial results, watch tracks and build-history queries. Each package is counted once; its Checks section lists the failed monitor and reason. An OBS build failure is a build result, not a failed collection check.</dd>
      <dt>Labels</dt>
      <dd>Labels link to packages with the same signal. Open a package for the provider evidence and collection checks; a security match does not evaluate local patches.</dd>
      <dt>Observation time</dt>
      <dd>Last updated is collection time; Succeeded at is build time. Failed checks retain earlier observations and their timestamps.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p><a href="/api/v2/status">Collection status</a> includes schedules, coverage and errors. The <a href="/api">query interface</a> exposes package observations as JSON.</p>
    <p><a href="/LICENSE.txt">MulanPSL-2.0 license</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/openRuyi-Project/openRuyi-logo">openRuyi logo</a> © 2026 ISCAS and openRuyi Project Contributors. Used unchanged under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</p>
    <p>Activity icons: <a href="https://github.com/primer/octicons">GitHub Primer Octicons</a>, used unchanged under the <a href="https://github.com/primer/octicons/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a>.</p>
    <details><summary>Octicons license</summary><pre>{octiconsLicense}</pre></details>
    <p>Build icons: <a href="https://fontawesome.com/">Font Awesome Free 6.7.2</a> by Fonticons, Inc., used unchanged under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.</p>
    <details><summary>Font Awesome notices</summary><pre>{fontAwesomeLicense}</pre></details>
    <h2>Tool and ecosystem marks</h2>
    <p>Marks identify tools or language families, not endorsement. GNU identifies the Autotools family; language marks do not identify a particular build backend.</p>
    <p>Python and the Python logos are trademarks or registered trademarks of the Python Software Foundation, used under its nominative-use policy.</p>
    <p>CMake is a Kitware trademark, used only to identify the build tool; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p>
    <dl class="api-list">
      {Object.values(logos).map(logo => <><dt><a href={logo.source}>{logo.title}</a></dt><dd>{logo.credit}. <a href={logo.license_url}>{logo.license}</a>. <a href={logo.asset_source}>SVG source</a>. {logo.changes} {'trademark_url' in logo && <a href={logo.trademark_url}>Trademark policy</a>}</dd></>)}
    </dl>
  </article>
</Base>
